{"title": "UZH-FPV", "parts": {"header": "<div class=\"sd ex-sd\"><div class=sd-grid><div class=sd-head><span class=\"sd-maker none\">UZH Robotics and Perception Group</span><h1 id=\"_top\">UZH-FPV</h1><p class=sd-type>Snapdragon Flight stereo + IMU</p></div><figure class=sd-plate><div class=sd-frame><img src=\"/media/examples/uzh-fpv/uzh-fpv-drone.jpg\" alt=\"The UZH-FPV racing quadrotor with its Snapdragon Flight board, mDAVIS346 camera and motion-capture prism\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\"></div><figcaption><a href=\"https://rpg.ifi.uzh.ch/docs/ICRA19_Delmerico.pdf\">Photo: UZH Robotics and Perception Group, Delmerico et al., ICRA 2019, Fig. 4</a></figcaption></figure><div class=sd-cta><div class=sd-buttons><a class=\"sd-btn primary\" href=\"https://fpv.ifi.uzh.ch/datasets/\">Downloads: UZH-FPV datasets page</a><a class=\"sd-btn\" href=\"/benchmark/results/uzh-fpv/\">MVIS: results page</a></div></div><div class=sd-specs><dl class=sd-rows><div class=sd-row><dt>Cameras</dt><dd>Snapdragon Flight: 2 × 640×480 global shutter</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>IMU</dt><dd>About 500 Hz</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Board</dt><dd>AprilGrid 5×4, tag 75 mm</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Format</dt><dd>ROS1 bag</dd></div><div class=sd-row><dt>Licence</dt><dd>see <a href=\"/about/license/#linked-uzh-fpv\">License</a></dd></div></dl></div></div></div>", "glance": "<p>One MVIS camera + IMU run on the Snapdragon Flight&#x27;s indoor 45° calibration recording, against the Kalibr calibration the dataset ships. Of the 8 UZH-FPV calibration bags, this is the one whose motion calibrates the IMU intrinsics and lever most reliably: see the digital-twin check on the results page.</p><div class=band><figure class=demo><video src=\"/media/hero/hero_uzhs_960.mp4\" poster=\"/media/hero/hero_uzhs_960.jpg\" autoplay muted loop playsinline controls preload=metadata></video><figcaption>The scene MVIS recovered from this dataset, as on the homepage. The values beside it come from this page&#x27;s run.</figcaption></figure><div class=v data-v=\"0\"><div class=tiles><div><span>Reprojection median</span><b>0.22<small> px</small></b></div><div><span>cam0–cam1 baseline</span><b>80.0<small> mm</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 td</span><b>−14.24<small> ms</small></b></div><div><span>cam0 lever arm</span><b>26.8<small> mm</small></b></div></div></div></div><p class=sd-note>Reprojection is how far, in pixels, the detected corners lie from where the solve puts them. td is the camera–IMU time offset, and the lever arm is the camera–IMU position offset.</p>", "process": "<p>MVIS's own player, from this run: the detected board corners, then the rig's path as the solve refines it. Press <b>Play</b> or drag the bar; pick a camera card to look through that camera. We publish no camera images.</p><div class=proc-wrap><button type=button class=proc-open hidden><svg viewBox=\"0 0 400 220\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><polygon points=\"101.5,159.7 210.1,200.0 298.5,167.3 189.9,127.0 101.5,159.7\" fill=\"var(--strong)\" fill-opacity=\".1\" stroke=\"var(--muted)\"/><polyline points=\"189.2,89.4 161.0,89.5 154.5,79.1 162.6,70.0 183.6,66.0 211.5,71.6 224.9,84.5 212.7,101.6 185.1,112.1 159.4,100.7 146.2,78.1 142.2,57.1 154.4,41.7 178.5,41.9 204.5,51.8 220.0,72.9 212.8,94.2 196.5,105.7 173.5,96.7 167.0,42.4 180.4,25.0 196.4,48.1 195.9,101.2 186.3,109.9 181.1,74.8 178.9,35.4 183.5,47.0 184.0,85.2 170.4,113.3 165.3,97.9 191.8,84.7 225.5,98.7 217.2,105.6 188.1,104.0 163.4,97.8 168.1,79.3 187.5,64.6 207.6,70.5 207.9,91.2 209.5,96.8 213.0,90.7 209.4,90.4 187.1,95.0 162.4,92.9 150.1,81.2 163.8,60.9 184.8,55.1 197.4,67.6 196.4,95.5 189.3,115.6 189.3,124.1 202.9,117.7 211.3,107.1 202.1,99.5 182.3,99.9 157.5,96.2 159.4,78.8 193.2,54.9 183.8,83.7 169.8,102.6 160.5,110.8 154.0,102.4 164.6,83.5 188.4,77.4 214.9,78.0 249.0,94.8 239.8,106.0 222.0,116.4 189.2,120.0 159.2,122.1 140.4,125.3 116.8,111.4 122.2,85.1 142.3,73.0 165.9,68.4 197.9,70.2 221.2,73.2 231.3,79.4 238.6,93.3 238.0,107.3 229.8,117.4 217.2,120.6 201.5,124.1 183.2,125.6 161.7,110.9 151.4,89.5 151.4,64.1 155.1,39.9 174.0,20.0 204.9,39.7 217.9,72.9 216.0,102.1 202.7,113.1 183.5,115.0 158.5,107.5 142.9,100.5 132.2,92.7 127.3,80.3 137.8,61.3 197.3,51.1 234.8,68.2 251.4,91.2 248.3,103.4 231.3,106.5 192.6,108.4 163.8,103.9 143.6,92.4 154.8,72.1 201.1,77.1 215.7,95.3 226.6,97.3 225.5,91.2 206.6,94.3 170.2,92.0 157.9,76.5 170.1,58.9 217.8,98.3 183.0,116.7 147.7,112.7 126.2,93.7 117.9,72.3 131.8,52.6 159.1,43.8 185.5,43.6 216.8,53.6 235.7,65.6 240.7,88.2 223.1,106.1 200.0,107.3 166.7,101.9 151.6,78.3 213.9,36.9 175.6,86.1 154.4,106.5 236.9,92.3 228.7,99.9 203.5,105.1 171.5,99.7 146.6,79.1 140.5,48.6 168.7,35.0 194.6,49.8 206.8,82.2 201.4,101.1 181.2,105.5 160.4,96.7 163.9,86.3 197.1,73.1 204.7,77.9 179.8,98.7 167.6,107.4 204.5,79.5 208.8,65.0 195.2,70.0 145.5,103.3 133.5,112.4 137.2,116.5 159.7,115.0 185.1,105.6 202.1,88.7 204.6,70.9 191.6,70.1 173.2,81.5 158.2,98.7 153.7,104.2 144.6,101.4 138.4,88.3 195.0,100.1 202.3,110.1 201.5,109.9 184.7,105.2 160.8,96.6 146.7,88.0 144.2,69.1 187.8,97.2 171.8,104.8 153.8,105.0 126.5,98.7 116.9,91.6 131.0,79.7 206.8,100.1 181.1,101.5 158.3,83.7 151.7,58.4 162.7,42.1 185.2,37.5 213.0,57.1 219.7,80.0 211.2,93.4 194.2,97.7 173.2,87.4 176.2,68.5 193.9,59.0 216.2,62.0 221.1,74.3 202.9,92.9 175.8,104.3 153.8,103.5 141.0,94.3 144.6,80.2\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></svg><span>Explore in 3D (about 1 MB)</span></button><div class=\"mvv\" data-mvv=\"scene\" data-mode=\"site\" data-src=\"/media/examples/uzh-fpv/views0.json\"></div></div>", "result": "<p>The solved positions and orientations, to scale in the IMU frame. Drag sideways to orbit. Tap a sensor to see its values.</p><div class=map><div class=stage><canvas id=rig tabindex=0 aria-label=\"3D map of the cameras and IMU\"></canvas><div class=tools><button data-view=iso type=button>3D</button><button data-view=front type=button>Front</button><button data-view=top type=button>Top</button><button data-view=side type=button>Side</button><button data-z=1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom in\">+</button><button data-z=-1 type=button aria-label=\"Zoom out\">−</button></div></div><div class=panel><div class=picks id=picks></div><div id=info></div></div></div><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Sensor</th><th>fx, fy, cx, cy px</th><th>Lever mm</th><th>log(R) rad</th><th>td ms</th><th>t_ga ms</th><th>Reprojection px</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th>cam0</th><td>276.3, 275.9, 314.7, 242.2</td><td>[+13.6, +22.9, −2.5]</td><td>[−1.7490, +1.7980, −0.7374]</td><td>−14.24</td><td></td><td>0.197</td></tr><tr><th>cam1</th><td>275.6, 275.2, 314.5, 235.0</td><td>[+12.3, −57.1, −3.2]</td><td>[−1.7436, +1.7846, −0.7255]</td><td>−14.27</td><td></td><td>0.246</td></tr><tr><th>IMU (base)</th><td></td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>−0.82 ± 0.10</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Lever arms and rotations are each sensor in the base IMU frame; rotation is log(R) in rad. td is the time offset to the base IMU, t_imu = t_sensor + td. Reprojection is the median per camera (all cameras: median 0.217 px): how well the model fits the corners, not how accurate it is.</p>", "check": "<p>Reference: <a href=\"https://fpv.ifi.uzh.ch/datasets/\">The Kalibr camera + IMU calibration shipped with this recording on the UZH-FPV datasets page</a>.</p><div class=scroll><table class=num><thead><tr><th>Value</th><th>MVIS</th><th>UZH (Kalibr)</th><th>Difference</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam0</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[+13.61, +22.92, −2.46]</td><td>[+7.51, +24.05, +5.77]</td><td>Δp 10.31 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−1.7490, +1.7980, −0.7374]</td><td>[−1.7470, +1.7937, −0.7347]</td><td>Δθ 5.27 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>276.30</td><td>275.46</td><td>Δfx +0.84 px</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−14.236</td><td>−14.849</td><td>Δtd +0.613 ms</td></tr><tr class=grp><th colspan=4>cam1</th></tr><tr><td>Lever mm</td><td>[+12.29, −57.06, −3.19]</td><td>[+6.71, −55.87, +4.23]</td><td>Δp 9.36 mm</td></tr><tr><td>log(R) rad</td><td>[−1.7436, +1.7846, −0.7255]</td><td>[−1.7417, +1.7802, −0.7233]</td><td>Δθ 5.13 mrad</td></tr><tr><td>fx px</td><td>275.64</td><td>274.46</td><td>Δfx +1.18 px</td></tr><tr><td>td ms</td><td>−14.272</td><td>−14.951</td><td>Δtd +0.679 ms</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class=note>Δp is the distance between the two lever arms. Δθ = ‖log(R<sub>a</sub><sup>T</sup> R<sub>b</sub>)‖, the angle between the two rotations. A reference, not ground truth: it was solved by another tool on the same kind of data.</p><p class=note>Kalibr held the intrinsics fixed at UZH&#x27;s camera-only calibration; MVIS refines them, which explains most of the Δfx.</p><p class=note>On this bag the shipped Kalibr lever is about 9 mm from our own Kalibr run with the same IMU weights and camera seed; MVIS is within 2.4 mm of that run. In rotation the three differ by about 5 mrad.</p>", "config": "<p>The marked lines are the choices that matter for this rig:</p><ul class=list><li><code>gravity</code>: The local gravity at Innovation Park Zürich, Dübendorf, Switzerland: 9.8070 m/s². Set your own local value.</li><li><code>site</code>: The alternative to gravity: the recording site. With gravity set it does not change g; it names the city in the report.</li><li><code>board</code>: The UZH board: AprilGrid 5×4, tag 75 mm, spacing 0.2.</li><li><code>camera_input.path</code>: Seed intrinsics: UZH&#x27;s own camera-only Kalibr calibration, equidistant lens. MVIS refines them in this solve.</li><li><code>solve.sigma_g</code>: IMU noise from the residuals of UZH&#x27;s own Kalibr results, as UZH publishes no measured density. The other three sigmas are set the same way.</li><li><code>solve.estimate_t_ga</code>: Estimates t_ga, the time offset between the gyroscope and the accelerometer.</li></ul><p class=note>This is the config of the run on this page, with every path cut to its file name; the gravity line gives the g the run used. Point the paths at your copy, and take the gravity for your site from the <a href=\"/reference/local-gravity/\">Local gravity</a> page.</p><p>The solve took about 1 min on one desktop. It writes <code>cam_imu.json</code>, a calibration YAML and a report beside the config.</p><dl class=ex-kv><dt>MVIS</dt><dd>MVIS 0.4.1, solve of 2026-11-26</dd><dt>Run date</dt><dd>2026-11-26</dd><dt>Data</dt><dd><a href=\"https://fpv.ifi.uzh.ch/datasets/\">UZH-FPV datasets page</a></dd><dt>Config</dt><dd><code>uzh_fpv_snapdragon_indoor_45_cam_imu.yaml</code>, above</dd><dt>Command</dt><dd><code>mvis cam-imu -c uzh_fpv_snapdragon_indoor_45_cam_imu.yaml</code></dd></dl>", "dataset": "<div class=two><div><ul class=list><li>Recording indoor_45_calib_snapdragon: the Snapdragon Flight&#x27;s two 640 × 480 global-shutter cameras, fitted with the equidistant lens model as in UZH&#x27;s own calibration, and its IMU at about 500 Hz. It is 46 s long.</li><li>IMU noise: UZH publishes no measured noise density, so the sigmas come from the residuals of UZH&#x27;s own Kalibr results. They are estimates.</li><li>Board: AprilGrid 5×4, tag 75 mm, spacing 0.2, t36h11.</li><li>Cite Delmerico et al., &quot;Are We Ready for Autonomous Drone Racing? The UZH-FPV Drone Racing Dataset&quot;, ICRA 2019.</li><li>Solve window: 42.7 s.</li></ul><p>Download: <a href=\"https://fpv.ifi.uzh.ch/datasets/\">UZH-FPV datasets page</a> The recordings are listed there, not copied here.</p></div><div><figure class=board><svg viewBox=\"-30.0 -30.0 495.0 405.0\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"AprilGrid 4 by 5, to scale\"><rect x=\"-30.0\" y=\"-30.0\" width=\"495.0\" height=\"405.0\" fill=\"#fff\"/><path fill=\"#111\" d=\"M-15.00 -15.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM75.00 -15.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM165.00 -15.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM255.00 -15.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM345.00 -15.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM435.00 -15.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM-15.00 75.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM75.00 75.00h15.00v15.00h-15.00zM165.00 75.00h15.00v